# Shell scripts must check out with LF line endings on every machine. On a
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true (for example GitHub's windows-latest
# runners), git converts LF to CRLF for text files, and bash then fails on
# the \r at each line end ("$'\r': command not found"). The Android build
# runs scripts/build-android-*.sh with Git for Windows' bash, also in CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
